   {
    "attributes": [
     {
      "_key": "227mFCOl8uclHuS5roWMZG",
      "name": "Why I'm standing",
      "value": "After nine years in parliament - three as the electorate MP - I have a track record of delivery for the Wairarapa electorate. I brought back state housing to Wairarapa and the Tararua District, secured new trains for the Wairarapa line, new roundabouts and funding for Route 52. I stood alongside the community to successfully fight the Government's plans to toll the Manawatu-Tararua Highway. I'm seeking your vote because I am motivated to do more."
     },
     {
      "_key": "227mFCOl8uclHuS5roWMc5",
      "name": "About me",
      "value": "I have proven that I fight for Wairarapa, the Tararua District and Central Hawke's Bay. And now that Ashhurst is within the electorate boundaries I will fight for them too. This government took money allocated to fix Wairarapa Hospital. The Minister ducked for cover. The local MP remained silent throughout. I kept fighting and eventually forced them to give it back. We need an electorate MP that pushes for our region at every opportunity."
     },
     {
      "_key": "227mFCOl8uclHuS5roWMeu",
      "name": "Priority 1",
      "value": "My passion is housing. Everyone deserves a warm, dry and secure place to call home."
     },
     {
      "_key": "227mFCOl8uclHuS5roWMhj",
      "name": "Priority 2",
      "value": "Wages that go up more than prices increase, with decent conditions. Otherwise, we just go backwards."
     },
     {
      "_key": "227mFCOl8uclHuS5roWMkY",
      "name": "Priority 3",
      "value": "Investment in the infrastructure that we need, from Featherston in the south to Waipawa in the north."
     }
    ],
